+## Sales and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number). Each dish sold uses one portion of its recipe per `qty`; the
+  ingredients are consumed at `soldAt` with the ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>`.
+  Tickets already in the ledger are skipped. The answer is
+  `{ "tickets": <tickets imported>, "dishes": <dishes sold, sum of qty> }`.
+  A bad row (`bad_request`) or an item running out (`sale_not_enough_stock`)
+  imports nothing; the message names the row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists
+  `{ itemId, theoretical, actual, difference }` per item for the days from
+  `from` to `to` (inclusive, by UTC day): `theoretical` is the use booked by
+  sales sold in those days, `actual` every `consume` movement in those days,
+  `difference` is `actual - theoretical`. Items where both are 0 are left out.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
